R&C patch 7051: the PSO preload key file records the GPU-fetch pipelines (load stalls, the RE notes s.30).
KZ3 patch 2031 records each PSO the walker builds in <shader cache dir>\pso_keys.bin so the next session's preload
recreates it before the walker asks. KZ3 2076 left out the GPU-fetch variant (packed payload mode 2), to be derived
from the packed (mode 1) record by the template prewarm. With LD_VTX_GPU=1 (R&C's default, rc_settings.h) the walker
never builds the mode 1 pipeline of a covered draw, so no mode 1 record exists, and the template prewarm runs only with
LD_PSO_TEMPLATE: the GPU-fetch pipelines were never preloaded. ToD stall-cold (2026-11-10, exe 196c72c2): 181 PSOs
built, 179 stored in the pipeline library, 20 keys in pso_keys.bin; stall-warm preloaded 20 and the walker awaited 161.
- A mode 2 build is recorded with the new LD_PL_FLAG_VGPU (its own key, VS hash and layout); the preload worker passes
  the record's packed mode to ld_pso_desc_fill (mode 2: one R32_UINT VGIDX input) and skips mode 2 records when
  LD_VTX_GPU is off this session. LD_PL_VERSION 3 -> 4: older builds (RSX_TRANSLATOR_ID is 0 in R&C) must not read
  mode 2 records as mode 1; a v3 file is discarded once with its pipeline library.
- The record flags and the append move to libs/video/rsx_pso_keys_rec.h (pure C). The append was already per key
  (open, write, close); it now reports a failed write. Host test port/rc/tests/run_pso_keys_rec_test.sh: flags, a
  writer SIGKILLed after 1/7/50/333 keys keeps them all with no torn record, and a negative control (one buffered FILE
  kept open) loses them on the same kill.

